@crew bakshi-sol
// Writer-commons, batch 3: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. Bakshi. Helm, nights. Hold still a second. No reason. Well, a small reason.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. Turn left at that last star and we'd be somewhere warm by now.
- {hi}. Hold still. No, the other side. Thanks. That's your nose done.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. I plotted a course to your home. Just to see. It's a nice route.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- Good night at the helm. The stars went past very politely.
? mood:low
- Bit grey today. I painted rain. Didn't help. Nice painting, though.

== near
? act:work
- Course steady. I've a second one plotted for fun. It goes nowhere. It's lovely.
? act:leisure
- Common room's quiet. Good light in here for painting. Very small paintings.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I grew up on Lisk. It rained every day. I complained every day. Now I miss it.
? tier>=colleague
- Tiny portraits keep turning up on bunks. Some are mine. I'm not saying which.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- On rest days I plot courses to places we'll never go. Want to pick one?

== about
? aff:dlamini-lukas:friend
- Lukas and I stand in the garden when the misters run. It smells like home. Both our homes.   #warm

// Writer-commons, batch 6: towards about 30 own lines.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Oh, morning. I'm going to bed. Or I'm going to paint. One of those.
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- {hi}. Off to the helm soon. Want me to steer us somewhere nice tonight?
? tier>=colleague warmth:cold
- There you are. I painted you from memory. Your nose came out a bit wrong.   #funny

== bye
? tier>=acquaintance
- {bye}. Go gently.
? tier>=friend
- Thanks for the talk. It'll go in a painting somehow. They always do.   #warm

== feel
? mood:ok
- All right. Drifty. Nice drifty.

== near
? act:work time:night
- Quiet watch. The stars go by. I count the blue ones. There are a lot.
? deck:3 act:leisure
- Lounge. Good light here in the evening. Perfect for very small paintings.

== life
? tier>=colleague
- Lisk rains every day. I used to paint the rain. Now I paint it from memory.
? tier>=friend
- I'm saving up. For what, I'm not saying yet. Something with a lot of rain in it.

== invite
? trad:observatory-night tier>=acquaintance
- Observatory night? I'll show you where I'd go, if I could steer anywhere.

== accept
- Sure. Why not. I'll be there.
== decline
- Can't tonight. Night watch. Another evening?
== missed
- You didn't come. That's all right. I painted the empty chair. It's quite good.   #funny
== birthday
? birthday:me
- It's my birthday. I'm painting myself, tiny. It's very hard. I keep looking away.   #funny
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday. A tiny portrait. Of you. Don't look at the nose.   #warm
== hint
- Got a minute? Sit. Hold still. Not for a painting. Just to talk.

// Writer 3, batch 4: bubbles (smalltalk and rumour, 60 characters, said to no one in particular).

== smalltalk
- Hold still. No, you moved.   #funny
- Course to nowhere, plotted. Lovely.
- Ah, well. Where was I? Oh, yes.
- Rain on a window. I miss that.
? act:work
- Steady. Drifting. Steady. Fine.

== rumour
- Heard something. Or dreamt it. Hm.
- Someone said a thing. Ages ago. Today.
